WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.390
Mr. Handa's Make-over Plan.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:41.550
Hey, do you know about 
your popularity period?

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.870
Popularity period <i>(moteki)</i>?

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.380
That would be a steam whistle <i>(kiteki)</i>.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.020
That would be target 
practice <i>(shateki)</i>.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:54.800
That would be a miracle <i>(kiseki)</i>.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.340
What do you mean by "popularity period"?

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.520
Everyone has a point in their life

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.240
when they become very popular

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:03.350
and that's a "popularity period."

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.870
Wouldn't that be breeding season?

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.060
I would think so.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.210
Apparently it's a little different.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:14.440
Breeding season only comes around 
when it's the right season,

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:17.600
your popularity period apparently comes
 when you work hard for it.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.590
What are you all talking about?

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.460
Watch this.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.280
Miss Sasako...

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:23.700
Yes?

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:26.370
Here.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.270
A mask?

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.820
Huh? Then how about...

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.090
Here you go.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.010
A carrot?

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.710
Huh? Then...

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.010
I weigh more than 100 kilograms.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.110
I see.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.170
Isn't that heavy?

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:52.920
It is.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.250
That's all?

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.340
Yes.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.140
How strange.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.980
I heard that in order to be 
popular, you had to have

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.370
a mask <i>(omen)</i>, vegetables <i>(yasai)</i>, 
and be heavy <i>(omoi)</i>.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.040
By chance do you mean,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.830
be good-looking <i>(ikemen)</i>, 
nice <i>(yasashii)</i>, and funny <i>(omoshiroi)</i>?

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.930
I guess I was a little off.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.670
You were close, though!

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.520
No, he got it completely wrong.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.410
Are you making a delivery?

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:34.420
What lovely flowers!

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.050
Thank you very much.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.110
That must be the popularity period.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.370
Well, I have to go deliver 
this to the shop.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.120
Aw, please don't leave!

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.480
M-My apologies.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.030
Oh, no, pardon me, as well.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:58.260
Are you okay?

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.050
Are you hurt?

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.300
No, I'm fine.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.480
Are you sure?

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.220
Yes.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.710
Thank goodness.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.790
I was so worried.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:08.680
Mr. Handa.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.440
I'll help you out.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.320
Don't worry, we'll figure it out.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.150
Oh, Panda! Good morning!

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:21.070
You don't need my help, Rin Rin.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.390
Come on, let's go, Mr. Handa.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:30.040
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:34.000
Hello! Hey, listen, listen!

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.750
What is it?

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.850
I finally got my temporary license!

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:39.880
Finally! At last!

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.230
Huh?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.840
Polar Bear's not here?

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.890
He said he had something 
important to do.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.600
You're going to do it here?

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.850
Help me out, Polar Bear.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.210
You're very determined, Panda.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.340
I've been gathering information.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:03.330
Sorry!

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:07.000
An older person was asking 
me for directions.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.240
Come on, let's go, Mr. Handa.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.200
Where to?

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:16.890
Mr. Handa's make-over plan!

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.210
First, let's start with fashion.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.720
Nonchalant trad.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.090
Hmm, seems a little too serious.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.430
How about punk?

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.690
I don't know about this either.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.400
What about Shibuya style?

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:43.610
Seems more subculture style.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:47.560
Ooh, this is it!

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:49.070
It's perfect.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.720
This is the same thing I always wear.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.790
Well, then...

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:01.220
For popular fashion,

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:04.590
we need to find you something that 
helps you proclaim your manliness.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.180
For a rooster, it'd be the cockscomb.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:12.120
For a cat, I think it'd be the ears.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.090
For birds, it'd be their feathers.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.350
But most importantly, there's this.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.820
A panda costume?

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:27.590
You see me all the time and 
you don't notice, Mr. Handa?

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:29.320
I'm really popular.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.820
What about this?

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.490
It's a little tight, though.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.330
You look like a panda, Polar Bear.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:42.750
Maybe I'll work at the zoo 
in your place, Panda.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.210
I don't think that's possible.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.970
You opened the package, 
so make sure you buy it.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.950
I didn't bring my wallet.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.350
Thank you very much!

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.460
Now, on to the next stop.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.530
Apparently, it's also important to 
know about gourmet foods.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.990
How's that important?

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.550
It's important for your 
life, Mr. Handa.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:15.990
I see...

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.120
Jeez, what's with the 
lack of enthusiasm?

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.520
And I'm trying so hard, too.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.920
They have a lot of 
delicious-looking stuff.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.260
Bamboo grass yeast cakes                                                 Bamboo grass dumplings

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.880
Bamboo grass yeast cakes                    Bamboo grass dumplings                    Bamboo grass red bean jelly

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:29.720
Bamboo grass yeast cakes,

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.980
bamboo grass dumplings,

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.510
bamboo grass red bean jelly!

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.990
You should buy it for him.

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:40.920
Looks like I don't have a choice.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.160
But just one.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.320
And this, too.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:01.500
Mr. Handa!

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:06.420
Mr. Handa!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.170
One hundred yen! One hundred yen!

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.500
What in the world are you 
doing, Polar Bear?!

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:17.880
You've got your hands full, Mr. Handa.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:19.140
You must be popular!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:23.530
Handa-san, you're well on your way
 to being remade, as a cyborg.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:25.900
No, that'd mean I'd have to fight.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:33.810
Let's go!

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:35.320
I wonder what that's about?

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:37.290
They're looking over here.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:39.890
E-Excuse me.

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:41.250
Yes?

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.240
If it's not too much trouble...

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.750
Could you take a picture 
with all of us?

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.710
Your popularity period has arrived!

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.310
Sure.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:55.090
Thank you!

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:00.110
You sure are popular, Panda.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:02.220
I'm going to get in the picture, too.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.820
I'm gonna take one more.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:07.900
Okay!

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:16.360
Wow, that sure was fun!

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.340
Welcome back.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:19.580
You were gone a long time.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.620
Pardon me, could you take our order?

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.620
Right away.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.340
There you go.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.760
Could I get some more water?

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:26.930
Coming right up!

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:30.070
It looks really busy.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:31.750
Miss Sasako...

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.050
sure is popular.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.890
Oh, hey, Mr. Handa.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.860
Pardon me, could I get some more water?

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:45.130
Oh, Mr. Handa! 
Could you scratch my back?

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:48.140
Mr. Handa!

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.650
Could you tell him not 
to sit on me please?

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.380
Sure thing.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.220
Thank you very much.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.070
Not a problem.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.370
Right here?

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.040
A bit to the right.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:06.140
Please sit here.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.000
Thank you.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.920
It's finally arrived for Mr. Handa.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.460
It sure has.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.330
His popularity period.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.040
Could I get another water, Mr. Handa?

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:17.920
Sure thing!

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:20.730
Could you scratch over 
here, too, Mr. Handa?

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:21.470
Sure!

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.550
Mr. Handa!

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:24.970
What is it?

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:29.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:29.330
The Great Love Love Driving Operation!

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.900
Look, look!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.310
I finally got it!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.750
Emperor Penguin

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.750
Driver's License

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.040
My license!

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:49.990
Good for you.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:50.710
Hey!

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.170
Congratulate me <i>(omedetou)</i>!

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.960
That's a small candy <i>(konpeitou)</i>!

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.710
That's the Eiffel Tower <i>(efferu tou)</i>!

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.140
Aikido

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.140
That's Aikido <i>(aikidou)</i>!

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.990
That's not it! That's not it at all!

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.660
Congratulations.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:09.600
Thank you!

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:11.270
Congratulations.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.350
Thanks!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:15.000
I thought you'd never get it.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.570
That's not even funny.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:20.870
Now I can take Miss Penko...

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:24.240
for a drive to the ocean!

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:28.630
I don't know if it'll be that easy.

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:30.880
Why?

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.170
For example...

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:36.390
You get lost and end 
up going to the mountains

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:38.260
instead of the ocean.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.920
You break the gear shift.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:49.600
The steering wheel comes off.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:56.290
No, I won't make any 
of those mistakes.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:59.190
But you're not just 
going on a drive, right?

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:02.510
It'll be a date.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.810
You'll have to make 
interesting conversation

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:06.740
with Miss Penko in the passenger seat

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.240
while not getting lost.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.420
Can you do that?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.280
That's quite a mission.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.960
I know! Let's go for a 
practice run tomorrow!

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:26.810
What do you do on a practice date?

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.560
I've got it all figured out.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.350
Good morning, Mr. Penguin.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.260
Huh?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.790
Miss Penko...

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:39.820
Mr. Penguin.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.280
Why are you sleeping here?

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:48.630
Well, I got here three hours ago.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.960
It's good that you're early, 
but very bad to be sleeping.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:56.920
No. 1, Meeting: Failed.

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:58.880
What's that?

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:01.050
A score card.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.840
If you don't pass, you don't 
get your dating license.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:08.110
You need a license for dating, too?

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:08.970
You do.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:12.060
No, you usually don't.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:16.020
I'll be your dating instructor 
today, Mr. Penguin.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.980
I-I know that.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:21.370
So, what's your plan for today?

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:23.250
We're going to the ocean!

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.400
That's it?

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:28.320
No dinner at a fancy restaurant,

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:30.910
or interesting plans to enhance the mood?

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:35.450
You didn't think about that, did you?

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.990
No. 2, Arrangements: Failed.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.890
It looks like the path to 
passing is very hard.

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:48.020
What else is on that check list?

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:50.590
No. 3, Fun Conversation.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:53.100
No. 4, Delicious Meal.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.680
No. 5, Romantic Mood.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.610
If you pass all of those, 
you'll receive a temporary license.

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:03.380
And after your love love drive,
 you confess your love.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:06.900
If you can do that, 
you'll receive a love love license.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.370
Love love license?

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:19.200
You've already failed two, though.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.870
Well then, let's start over.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:24.720
Okay.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:28.050
Good morning. Were you waiting long?

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.090
Good morning.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.550
I just got here, too.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.610
Very nice. You passed.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.980
So what are we doing?

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:42.100
First we'll go to a delicious restaurant, 
then to the ocean,

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:44.940
then I'll enhance the mood, 
and then I'll confess my love, Instructor!

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:48.420
A bit awkward, but I guess you pass.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.910
Let's go, then.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.180
I feel tired.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:55.470
Can you drive, Polar Bear?

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:57.370
That's a no.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.370
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.170
Oh, I forgot my snacks.

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:14.260
Do you have any, Mr. Penguin?

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.730
Don't talk to me. It's distracting.

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.860
Oh yeah, the other day...

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.190
I just told you not to talk to me.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:29.440
No. 3, Fun Conversation: Failed.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.830
You have to enhance the mood more.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:38.130
But it's hard to enhance the 
mood when it's three guys.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:43.500
You're the one that said you 
wanted to do a practice run.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.370
I know, but...

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:47.090
Looks like you've left me no choice.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:57.240
Wow, what beautiful scenery.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:58.510
What are you doing?

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:01.830
I'll pretend to be Miss Penko.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:05.940
So you're a girl from 
now on, Polar Bear?

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:11.020
I forgot my sunblock.

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:16.520
Hey, that's not going to work.

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:18.870
What should I say?

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:22.250
First you need to compliment me.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.860
Just compliment me.

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:25.330
O-Okay.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:29.300
Y-You're so fair-skinned 
and pretty, Miss Polar Bear.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:32.470
Oh, stop, Mr. Penguin.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.810
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:39.810
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:45.270
I seem to have gained a 
little bit of weight lately.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:47.130
I see.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.440
You see?

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:57.660
Chubby girls like you are 
much cuter, Miss Polar Bear.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.430
Really?!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.830
Miss Polar Bear, your nails! Your nails!

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:05.330
Oh dear.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:10.300
I'm sorry, did my nails hurt?

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.800
Of course it hurt!

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:18.710
Your nails are so sturdy, 
they're truly fantastic.

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:20.260
Really?

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.770
Really. Really.

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:25.770
No. 3, Fun Conversation: Passed.

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.300
Good for you, Mr. Penguin.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.080
What should we do for lunch?

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.360
I want bamboo grass!

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:39.330
Somewhere that Miss Penko would like.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.620
It's fresh!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.620
Conveyor Belt Sushi

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.620
Isshin Tarou

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.620
Isshin

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:46.040
There's no bamboo grass.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:49.480
This isn't much of a restaurant.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.410
When it's the real thing,

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:54.250
we'll be going to a fancy 
seafood restaurant!

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:56.370
Excuse me.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:58.760
I'd like some salmon.

00:17:58.760 --> 00:17:59.970
Sorry, we're out.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:06.320
You ate all of the salmon 
in the place, Polar Bear.

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.730
Well then, let's go.

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:12.130
Of course, you're paying, Mr. Penguin.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:12.690
What?

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:18.150
You were going to make 
a girl pay on the date?

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:20.630
That's unbelievable.

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:21.660
All right, fine.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:32.880
Isshin 
Tarou

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:25.560
No. 4, Delicious Meal: 
I passed that, right?

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:30.700
Conveyor belt sushi 
feels strange for a date.

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:32.880
After you ate all that?!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:36.710
All right, we'll say you passed.

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.390
There's no... conversation.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.920
I already passed that section.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:51.340
This is where it's important.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:53.330
You have to enhance the mood.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.610
How?

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.640
When the conversation is paused,

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.080
you need something like background music.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:18:59.570
I didn't bring any CDs.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.170
Then I'll sing.

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:11.490
Sleep, sleep, in your mother's embrace.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:15.630
Sleep, slee—

00:19:16.980 --> 00:19:19.740
You're not supposed to fall 
asleep, Mr. Penguin!

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:23.680
Why would you sing a lullaby?!

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:27.640
I can't give you a passing 
grade at this rate.

00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:30.080
So he fails?

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.980
The ocean will enhance the mood!

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:34.610
Especially for penguins!

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:38.880
It's the ocean!

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.070
It's a bit far, though.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.410
I went the wrong way.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:50.120
Hey, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.830
One hundred yen! One hundred yen!

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:54.790
You don't need to look at it anymore.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:59.590
Seriously. How could you have 
gone the wrong way?

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:03.360
Miss Penko will get mad and go home.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.830
It'll be okay, this is 
just a practice run.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:10.480
If we go now, the sun will be 
setting across the ocean.

00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:13.440
It'll be romantic, no matter what!

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.850
It's the ocean!

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:19.400
Welcome to Sunset Beach

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.290
But...

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:25.030
We missed the sunset.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:30.790
No. 5, Romantic Mood: Failed.

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:33.750
I-Isn't the night scenery pretty, too?

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:35.710
See?

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:37.920
The mood is getting better!

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:41.600
Then do you want to 
move on to the confession?

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:46.350
Go for it.

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:50.030
Now, Mr. Penguin.

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:54.300
Tell me how you really feel 
about me, passionately.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:57.200
M-Miss Penko...

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:00.660
I've always loved you.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:01.820
Would you...

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:04.250
Would you...

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.740
go out with me?

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:12.660
Yes.

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:21.060
Ow!

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:22.440
You did it!

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:26.760
Even though it's practice, 
that was nerve-wracking.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:30.640
Well, let's say you passed.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.850
Here, your love love license.

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.720
Yay!

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:37.770
Congratulations!

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:01.920
Oh, Mr. Penguin.

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:04.380
How was your date?

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:06.510
Here you go. Enjoy.

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:07.840
Thank you very much.

00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:10.670
So, how was your date?

00:22:10.670 --> 00:22:11.880
We didn't go.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:17.030
Well, it's not summer yet.

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:19.600
It's not the right season 
for a drive to the ocean.

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:23.630
That's no good.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:24.520
Next Time

00:23:58.440 --> 00:24:00.540
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:02.320
What, Panda?

00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:03.690
How can I get

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:07.960
idols to confess their love 
 without me having to work?

00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:09.970
Well, that's really impudent.

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:12.150
Let's finish it, Polar Bear.

00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:14.880
Next time on Polar Bear's Café...

00:24:16.210 --> 00:24:18.430
versus Cambrian Palace....

00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:20.510
How about just Polar Bear's Café?

00:24:20.510 --> 00:24:21.970
Enjoy!

00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:24.520
A Magazine Interview Comes By
Salmon Hunter: Mr. Grizzly
